## Summary

**What landed** — the task premise was partly stale: settings.ui already had a "Tabs" page grouping all five options, so nothing needed moving (QSettings keys unchanged). The real work:

- **settings.ui**: renamed "Tabs" → "Tab Settings", added a `tabBarPosition` combo (Top/Bottom/Left/Right) with label buddy + tabstop.
- **settings.cpp**: load/save `tabs/tabBarPosition` (clamped to combo range), and `saveToSettings` now also calls `loadSettings()` on every live `TabWidget` — not just WebViews — so position changes apply to open windows without restart.
- **tabwidget.cpp**: `loadSettings()` maps the setting to `setTabPosition(North/South/West/East)`; out-of-range values fall back to North.
- **tabbar.cpp**: tear-off drag now uses the direction perpendicular to the strip (up/down/left/right per shape, was hardcoded "drag up"), and `tabSizeHint` bounds the transposed long axis so long titles can't stretch a vertical strip.

**Empirical finding**: Qt 6.11 gives corner widgets 0×0 geometry under West/East — so the corner "+" and shared close button hide while the bar is vertical (New Tab stays reachable via File menu, AddTab shortcut, context menu, double-click). Documented in ChangeLog.

