## What shipped

**Consent-gated remote filter lists** — the seeded EasyList/EasyPrivacy/uBlock subscriptions no longer auto-download on first run or when stale. `AdBlockSubscription::loadRules()` skips the refresh until `AdBlock/remoteListsConsent` is granted; consent comes from a one-shot first-launch prompt (`maybePromptForListConsent` in `postLaunch`), enabling the blocker, pressing "Update Subscription", or accepting an `abp:` subscribe link. `load()` writes `m_enabled` directly so startup can't silently grant.

**Chromium kill-list** — `applyChromiumFlags()` now always appends `--disable-background-networking --disable-component-update --disable-domain-reliability --disable-metrics --disable-sync --no-first-run`, and was moved to before the `BrowserApplication` ctor since the engine latches `QTWEBENGINE_CHROMIUM_FLAGS` at profile setup.

**`--telemetry-smoke`** — a raw-socket capture proxy listens from before the ctor (a `QTcpServer` can't exist that early — this caught a real coverage gap where ctor-time fetches went unobserved), the app-side NAM is routed through it via settings, and a Linux `/proc` scan catches process-owned sockets that bypass proxies. Fails on any hit within 30s.

**Bug found by the new test** — `rulesDownloaded()` wrote the downloaded list to a `QFile` that stayed open; `loadRules()` then re-read it as empty and cleared `lastUpdate`, so remote lists never persisted at all. Now closes the file before reloading.

