## What was wrong
Tools > Web Inspector and context-menu "Inspect Element" triggered `QWebEnginePage::InspectElement`, but Qt WebEngine renders DevTools into a page bound via `setDevToolsPage()` — no page was ever bound, so the action silently no-oped.

## Fix
- New `DevToolsWindow` (`src/devtoolswindow.{h,cpp}`): a shared, lazily-created top-level window hosting a `QWebEngineView`.
  - The DevTools page is created on the **inspected page's own profile** (recreated on profile change — private/Tor windows work).
  - Forces `JavascriptEnabled` on it — the Safest security tier disables JS profile-wide, which would blank the DevTools frontend.
  - Re-points the binding to the current page on each invocation (tab switches), tracks the inspected title, unbinds on close (`WA_DeleteOnClose`), and closes itself when the inspected page dies.
- `browsermainwindow.cpp`: Tools > Web Inspector routes through `DevToolsWindow::inspectElement()`.
- `webview.cpp`: context menu swaps the bare `pageAction(InspectElement)` for an action routed through the host — including the stock entry inside the `createStandardContextMenu()` fallback path. `devtools:` was already whitelisted by SEC02's `isBrowserHandledScheme`.

## Verified
- New `autotests/devtools` suite: **8/8 PASS** — binding on correct profile, `devtools://` frontend actually loads (`loadFinished`), rebinding across pages, Tools-menu end-to-end, close-releases-binding, inspected-page-death cleanup.
