## Implementation

- **`src/popupblocker.{h,cpp}`** — singleton gate: `shouldBlock()` consults the `websettings/blockPopupWindows` flag (same key the Privacy checkbox owns), scheme-gates to http/https, and checks a `popupExceptions/allowed` host list with parent-domain matching plus a session-only overlay for off-the-record pages.
- **`src/webpage.{h,cpp}`** — `createWindow` now decides by `WebWindowType`: `WebBrowserWindow`/`WebDialog` dead-end into a `PopupProbePage` (rejects all navigation, reports the first http/https/ftp target, self-reaps in 30s); tab shapes still follow `openTargetBlankLinksIn`. Per-document `blockedPopupCount()`/`blockedPopupUrls()` + `popupBlocked()` signal, reset on real navigations (fragment/same-doc survive). The `JavascriptCanOpenWindows` binding stays as the upstream gesture-less layer.
- **`src/locationbar/popupblockerbutton.{h,cpp}`** — count-badged indicator right of the adblock button: menu shows blocked count, per-target "Open" entries (new tab), "Always allow pop-ups on host", and a settings deep-link.
- **SitePanel** — new "Allow pop-ups on this site" checkbox writing the exception list.
- **Settings** — popup exceptions appear in the Privacy remembered-permissions tree (`popup|host` keys, removable, Clear-All covered); checkbox tooltip + hint text updated.
- **Docs** — ChangeLog section, README feature paragraph, WORKLOG line, task row → `done`.

## Verification

- `tst_popupblocker` 9/9, `tst_webpage` 45/45 (incl. **popupClickBlocking** — real synthetic click on the render delegate → `window.open('…','width=200,height=200')` arrives as `WebDialog` → blocked, target `/popup.html` captured), `tst_sitepanel` 15/15, `tst_settingsdialog` popupExceptions PASS.
- `make check` green: check-warnings PASS + 57 programs, 0 failed, offscreen `LIBGL_ALWAYS_SOFTWARE=1` (the plain-offscreen tst_webview SIGTRAP is the pre-existing env issue documented in UIP04's notes).
- `arora --quit-after-load https://www.kephyr.com/popupkillertest/test/index.html` → exit 0.

One finding worth noting: a feature-string `window.open` reports as **WebDialog** (not `WebBrowserWindow`) in Qt 6.12 — gating both shapes was essential. Stopping here per the one-task rule.
