## Stall mechanism (named, per task requirement)

Not QSettings-on-IO-thread and not the rust mutex (native matcher build, all reads already lock-snapshotted). The real chain:

1. uBO rules carry constraint options the parser silently ignored — `from=`, `to=`, `method=`, `ip=`, `cname`, `3p`. Dropping a constraint *widened* the rule: `*$script,redirect-rule=noopjs,from=dutchycorp.*,to=~sentry-cdn.com` became a redirect-every-script filter.
2. Its `arora-resource:/noop.js` target was fed back through the same interceptor, matched the same globalized rule again → redirect-chain churn; globalized `$image,3p` rules also blocked every image. Renderer spun at ~50–100% CPU while `Chrome_IOThread` sat idle in `ep_poll`.

## Fix (two legs)

- **Scheme gate** — `AdBlockRequestInterceptor::isWebRequestScheme()` admits only `http`/`https`/`ws`/`wss`; all three interceptors (adblock, privacy, Tor) early-return everything else — `devtools:`, `chrome:`, `qrc:`, `arora-*:`, `abp:`, `data:`, `file:` etc. pass untouched, and stub redirect targets can never re-enter the matcher.
- **Fail-closed parser** — `from=`, `to=`, `method=`, `ip=`, `cname`, `inline-script`, `inline-font`, `permissions=`, `popunder`, `urlrewrite` now mark a rule inert instead of broadening it. Aliases now parse correctly: `3p`/`1p`/`~3p`/`~1p`, `frame`/`doc`/`beacon`, `ehide`/`ghide`, `queryprune`.

Note: the resumed session found a leftover `// TEMP negative-control` edit that had dropped `from`/`to`/`method`/`ip`/`cname`/`inline-*`/`permissions` from the unsupported list — restored before commit (this is what the new test rows caught).

## Verification

- Negative control (fix reverted): **0/3** loads in 10 s
- Fixed binary, `.devin/stall01-repro.sh`: **30/30** (3 real pages × 10 iterations, each <10 s, seeded hostile list incl. a deliberately global `*$script` redirect)
- Real `/tmp/stall-home` corpus: Wikipedia `loadFinished` rc=0
- New autotest coverage: `webSchemeGate`, `selfRedirectTerminates` + 15 parser rows — tst_adblockrule 136/136, tst_adblockrequestinterceptor 10/10
- `make check`: rc=0, zero compiler warnings, all programs 0 failed

