## What shipped

**Registrable-domain emphasis** — when the location bar displays a URL (unfocused, unselected, unscrolled), `LocationBar::paintEvent` repaints the text row dimming the scheme/userinfo/subdomain/port/path to the Disabled/Text color while the eTLD+1 stays full-strength. `registrableDomainRange()` parses the encoded URL text for the domain span. Since Qt6 dropped `QUrl::topLevelDomain`/the PSL, `co.uk`-style registry boundaries ride the existing cookiejar `twoleveldomains_p.h` table; IP literals, localhost, and too-short hosts emphasize whole. `focusOutEvent` homes the cursor so the repaint's segment math lines up with QLineEdit's drawn text.

**IDN homograph display** — the bar already stores `url.toEncoded()` so punycode renders natively; a new `event(QEvent::ToolTip)` override + `unicodeUrlHint()` surfaces the decoded Unicode URL via `QToolTip` when the host differs from its ACE form.

