## What was done

Two privacy toggles riding the existing interceptor snapshot pattern:
- **`privacy/blockPrefetch`** (default ON) — blocks `ResourceTypePrefetch`
- **`privacy/blockRemoteFonts`** (default OFF, opt-in — icon fonts break) — blocks `ResourceTypeFontResource`

Both live in `PrivacyRequestInterceptor::shouldBlockResource()` behind the lock-guarded snapshot, consulted by the normal and Tor interceptors, with Privacy-tab checkboxes wired through settings load/save.

## Key finding

The e2e fixture caught a real gap the type check alone would have missed: **speculation-rules prefetch navigations arrive classified as `ResourceTypeMainFrame`** — indistinguishable from a link click (same `nav=LinkClicked`, empty initiator). But every prefetch flavor carries a `Purpose`/`Sec-Purpose: prefetch` request header, so the decision matches the header too. Verified empirically that no engine-side kill switch exists (`--disable-features=SpeculationRules` and `--disable-blink-features=SpeculationRules` both left the load alive).

## Verification

- `--resourceblock-smoke` (new 3-phase loopback fixture): armed → font + both prefetch flavors never reach the wire; fonts-off → font lands, prefetch still dead; both-off → prefetch lands (non-vacuous control)
