## Summary

**CONT02 — Per-tab container assignment + tab UI** is done. The interrupted run had the implementation nearly finished; this run fixed two test-design bugs, completed verification, and did the bookkeeping.

### Fixes made this session
- **`containerChipIndicator` test**: the assertion `tabRect(1) > tabRect(0)` could never hold — `QTabBarPrivate::layoutTabs` gives every tab the same `maxExtent` height. Corrected to compare against the pre-chip plain height, and the test stays unshown to avoid the offscreen GPU SIGTRAP.
- **`tabCookieIsolation` race**: `CookieJar` mirrors were created *after* the page load, so `loadAllCookies()` could snapshot before Chromium committed the cookie. Jars are now constructed before loading, and the test server records cookie headers per request target so an in-flight favicon request can't satisfy the assertion.
- Removed the leftover `fprintf` debug instrumentation from `containerChipSize`.

### Shipped feature
- `WebView::containerId()` resolves the page profile; `TabWidget::makeNewTabInContainer` + inherit-current-container new tabs; child windows keep the opener's container; private/Tor windows excluded.
